# Generation 3, round 4, X-09 (generations/gen003/PLAN.md, version 4, the second wide screen). Route (b), DEV-informed
# (LESSONS 44 and 48). Market-state continuation. x = the coin's k-day log return (3 weeks) in units of its own
# annualised daily volatility over the same k days; s = the sign of BTC's ls-day log return (8 weeks); both sampled
# at the last hour of each weekly bin. After a rising market (s = +1) long the recent winners and short the losers;
# after a falling market (s = -1) the reverse. The book stays in the market in both states. Rank weights, dollar
# neutral, gross 1, traded at the Monday 00:00 open. No funding, mark or index input.
name = "gen003_x09_state_continuation"
family = "trend"
kind = "portfolio"
unit = "top30"
hypothesis = "Market states and momentum: after a rising market, overconfident traders and inflows chase recent winners, so relative moves continue; after a falling market, deleveraging overshoots in the losers, which rebound hardest. Continuation of the 3-week relative move when BTC's 8-week return is positive, reversal when it is negative, weekly. DEV-informed. Falsified if the DEV screen fails (sign never flipped), VAL PSR(0) < 0.90, 2x costs negative, no G6 timing, or next30 disagrees."

k = param(21, 16, 26)          # days of the coin's relative move (3 weeks)
ls = param(56, 44, 68)         # days of BTC's return that set the state (8 weeks)

d = daily(close)
x = tf_last(logret(d, k) / realised_vol(d, k), weekly)
s = tf_last(sign(logret(daily(btc(close)), ls)), weekly)
signal = cs_scale(cs_demean(s * cs_rank(x)))
